Measure captured CUDA-graph memory by the allocator's reserved bytes instead of the driver's free-memory delta, and log the driver delta beside it. The graphs live in the allocator's private pool, so reserved bytes measure them on every platform; the driver delta also counts whatever else moved during capture.

Measured on 0.29.0 with the pool read both ways at the same two points: native RTX 3090, driver delta 0.11 GiB on the default profile and 0.24 on the KVarN huge-context profile; WSL2 RTX 4090, allocator delta 0.09 and 0.23 on the same profiles, cold or warm, while the driver's free-memory reading there is pinned at zero once the KV cache fills the budget (so the logged "actual" pool read 0.0) and collapses from 5.44 GiB to zero during the first compile of the KVarN kernels on a cold cache, which the graph-memory estimate then subtracted from the KV budget (5.44 GiB estimated for a 0.23 GiB pool) and refused the boot at -0.97 GiB available. The estimate's own capture over-reserves about 1 GiB on the default profile on both platforms with either reading (its capture is larger than the real one); that is unchanged here.

